pth_limit": 0, "concurrency_limit": 0, "budget": 0}, "by_type": {"implementer": 1}}, "safety_stops": 0, "is_error": false, "num_turns": 2, "subtype": "success", "api_error_status": null, "result": "`llm logs` now shows server-executed tool results. I ran the spec's check myself and it passes (`tests/test_llm_logs.py` and `tests/test_plugins.py`, 93 passed). The implementer reported the full suite also passes (1086), but I didn't run that.\n\n- **What changed:** results from the turn's output messages are collected alongside the input ones. Every tool call and result now carries a `server_executed` key. In Markdown, server results appear under `## Response`, after `### Tool calls` and before the response text. Local results stay in the prompt section. They also show up in `--json` and `--short`.\n- **Files:** `llm/logs.py`, `llm/cli.py` and `docs/changelog.md`, as the spec listed. I only checked the diffstat and the test run, not the code line by line.\n- **One addition beyond the spec:** the tool-instance lookup in `log_row_extras` now covers both input and output results, so server results can get their tool instance too.", "ttft_ms": 6909, "type": "result", "duration_ms": 29151, "uuid": "3fada5f6-a4d5-4b5c-b2a8-46a1ccf577e0", "ttft_stream_ms": 6361, "time_to_request_ms": 20, "first_content_frame_ms": 6361, "queued_turn_count": 0, "result_index": 1}
